You weaklings are no match for nothing.

00:26:22.600 --> 00:26:23.020
Yeah.

00:26:48.140 --> 00:26:57.050
- So there's really nothing left, Sasami?

00:26:57.050 --> 00:26:58.130
- What is this?

00:27:00.350 --> 00:27:03.670
No more snacks for a while. We're almost out of food.

00:27:03.670 --> 00:27:08.960
I see. We'll have to ask Keone to stop and do some grocery shopping, I guess.

00:27:12.790 --> 00:27:26.160
I wonder what's going on Keone.

00:27:26.160 --> 00:27:30.000
How can you be so unaware? Engine power's now going down.

00:27:30.280 --> 00:27:32.880
Well, what's the matter?

00:27:32.880 --> 00:27:35.270
Hey, what are you doing in here?

00:27:35.270 --> 00:27:37.770
It sounds like the engine's about to stop, you guys.

00:27:37.770 --> 00:27:40.830
I know that. I'm working on it right now.

00:27:40.830 --> 00:27:43.530
Keone, I told you you should learn to relax.

00:27:43.530 --> 00:27:45.810
And you should learn to panic!

00:28:01.050 --> 00:28:02.170
It's broken.

00:28:18.110 --> 00:28:28.800
There.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:35.250
clear for you. I'm a scientist, not a mechanic. Now I have some research to do, so if you'll

00:28:35.250 --> 00:28:40.710
excuse me. Wait, Washu. I mean Professor Washu, the greatest scientist in the universe.

00:28:40.710 --> 00:28:47.190
I know you can do it. Yes, you're a genius, and I agree with Keone, Washu. The greatest

00:28:47.190 --> 00:28:52.470
genius in the universe should be able to do this. Since you put it that way, fixing engine

00:28:52.470 --> 00:28:58.660
trouble should be a piece of cake. Redoxo, you're a genius, Washu.

00:28:59.890 --> 00:29:00.000
Thank you.

00:29:13.370 --> 00:29:14.310
so easy to please.

00:29:14.490 --> 00:29:15.090
No kidding.

00:29:16.770 --> 00:29:18.850
Hey, be quiet, will ya?

00:29:19.170 --> 00:29:21.020
Ha, here they are.

00:29:21.080 --> 00:29:21.640
I got them.

00:29:31.060 --> 00:29:43.820
I'm going to use an S32 plug here.

00:29:44.820 --> 00:29:47.470
Now I need some adhesive.

00:29:47.970 --> 00:29:49.010
Where is that adhesive?

00:29:49.290 --> 00:29:50.200
Where are you adhesive?

00:29:51.250 --> 00:29:52.840
Is this what you need?

00:29:53.370 --> 00:29:54.650
Oh, thank you, Mihoshi.

00:29:55.050 --> 00:29:58.000
I just stabilize this and then I...
